    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d264">

                <pb facs="0400" n="288" sameAs="frus:frus1910/pg288"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 893.772/1054.</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Minister Calhoun to
                        the Secretary of State.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >American Legation</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Peking</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian" when="1910-08-03"
                                ><hi rendition="#italic">August 3, 1910</hi></date>.</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 59.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: Having reference to the department’s
                    telegram of June 28, and to the legation’s telegrams of July 9 and 14,<anchor
                        n="1" xml:id="d264-f1"/> in reply thereto, all relating to the Hukuang loan
                    agreement, I have the honor to transmit herewith copy of the identic note of
                    July 13 presented to the Wai-wu-Pu by the English, German, French, and American
                    legations, and also a copy of the note presented on the same date by the English
                    and American legations, the two notes relating to the aforesaid agreement.</p>
                <p>I have, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">W. J. Calhoun.</hi></signed></closer>



                <xi:include href="d264-a1.xml" xpointer="d264-a1"/>
                <xi:include href="d264-a2.xml" xpointer="d264-a2"/>
